What is Data masking, how to implement this for PII or securities data in test automation explain with example 

**Data masking** = replacing real sensitive data (PII, account numbers, positions) with fake but realistic values so tests run without exposing actual data.

**In Selenium, it applies in 3 places:**
1. **Test data:** use masked/synthetic data, never real PII
2. **Logs/reports:** mask values before logging or attaching to reports
3. **Screenshots/UI validation:** verify the app masks fields (e.g., SSN shows `***-**-1234`)

**Example (Java + Selenium + TestNG)**

```java
// MaskUtil.java: masking helpers
public class MaskUtil {
    public static String maskSSN(String ssn) {
        return ssn.replaceAll("\\d{3}-\\d{2}-(\\d{4})", "***-**-$1");
    }
    public static String maskAccount(String acct) {
        return "*".repeat(acct.length() - 4) + acct.substring(acct.length() - 4);
    }
    public static String maskEmail(String email) {
        return email.replaceAll("(^.).*(@.*$)", "$1***$2");
    }
}
```

```java
// TestDataFactory.java: synthetic data via Faker
import com.github.javafaker.Faker;

public class TestDataFactory {
    private static final Faker faker = new Faker();
    public static String name()    { return faker.name().fullName(); }
    public static String email()   { return "user_" + faker.number().digits(6) + "@example.com"; }
    public static String account() { return faker.number().digits(12); }
}
```

```java
// CustomerTest.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.testng.Assert;
import org.testng.annotations.*;

public class CustomerTest {
    WebDriver driver;

    @BeforeClass
    public void setup() { driver = new ChromeDriver(); }

    @Test
    public void createCustomerAndVerifyMasking() {
        String name = TestDataFactory.name();
        String email = TestDataFactory.email();
        String account = TestDataFactory.account();

        driver.get("https://test-app.example.com/customer");
        driver.findElement(By.id("name")).sendKeys(name);
        driver.findElement(By.id("email")).sendKeys(email);
        driver.findElement(By.id("account")).sendKeys(account);
        driver.findElement(By.id("save")).click();

        // Log only masked values
        System.out.println("Created account: " + MaskUtil.maskAccount(account));

        // Validate the UI masks the account number
        String shown = driver.findElement(By.id("accountDisplay")).getText();
        Assert.assertEquals(shown, MaskUtil.maskAccount(account));
    }

    @AfterClass
    public void teardown() { driver.quit(); }
}
```

